      "message": "I looked up the behavior of the global `errno` behavior in this scenario:\n\n\"When using C++ std::fstream with exceptions enabled, errno is not guaranteed to be reliable or preserved inside a catch block.By default, std::fstream fails silently. If you intentionally enable exceptions via .exceptions(), the thrown std::ios_base::failure can trigger intermediate cleanup or platform-specific teardown code before your catch block runs. This secondary internal processing can overwrite the global errno value.\"",
